package domain

// Rules maps the ID of every sync rule to one English sentence that says what
// the rule does. An ID is R-<GROUP>-<NN> and is never renumbered or reused:
// plan operations name the rule they follow by its ID, and a test that
// exercises a rule names it in a "covers:" comment.
var Rules = map[string]string{
	"R-LINK-01": "An asset new in iCloud with no file in the cloud is uploaded to the cloud.",
	"R-LINK-02": "A file new in the cloud with no asset in iCloud is imported into iCloud.",
	"R-LINK-03": "An asset and a file that are both new are matched first and linked without a transfer when they match, otherwise each follows R-LINK-01 or R-LINK-02.",
	"R-LINK-04": "An album or library change in iCloud with an unchanged cloud file moves the file to its new event directory or root while the asset is in an event album.",
	"R-LINK-05": "A file moved or renamed in the cloud with an unchanged asset moves the asset to the album of its new folder.",
	"R-LINK-06": "New content in a cloud file with an unchanged asset replaces the asset in iCloud with one imported from the file.",
	"R-LINK-07": "Different changes to the same property on both sides are a conflict resolved by the conflict policy.",
	"R-LINK-08": "An asset trashed or deleted in iCloud with an unchanged cloud file applies the deletes policy to the cloud.",
	"R-LINK-09": "A file deleted in the cloud with an unchanged asset applies the deletes policy to iCloud.",
	"R-LINK-10": "A change in iCloud beats a deletion in the cloud: the file is uploaded again at its new place, with a warning.",
	"R-LINK-11": "A change in the cloud beats a deletion in iCloud: the file is imported as a new asset, with a warning.",
	"R-LINK-12": "A link deleted on both sides is cleared from the state.",
	"R-LINK-13": "The same change on both sides is not a conflict: the base takes it without operations.",
	"R-LINK-14": "Changes to different properties on the two sides, such as a new album in iCloud and new content in the cloud, are both applied.",

	"R-OBJECT-01": "An asset counts as deleted from a remote only when all its active links with the original or the source role there are gone.",
	"R-OBJECT-02": "When one of several links of an asset disappears, the asset leaves the album of that folder and is not deleted.",
	"R-OBJECT-03": "An asset gets a copy of one of its files in a remote, with its Live Photo video and RAW file but not its sidecars, as a new link in each directory it needs there that holds none of its files and that no file of it moves to, and it needs the directory of each of its event albums and no other.",
	"R-OBJECT-04": "A file of an asset left over in a remote once the directories the asset needs there have their files, such as the copy in an album that the asset left or that was deleted, moves to quarantine without a link, whatever the deletes policy.",
	"R-OBJECT-05": "While an asset is in an event album, a file of it under the root of its library but outside the directories it needs moves into one of them that holds none of its files instead of being copied there and quarantined, as when the asset leaves one event album for another.",
	"R-OBJECT-06": "An asset in no event album needs no directory in a remote, so every file of it there whose link names an album is left over and goes by R-OBJECT-04, as when the asset leaves its last event album.",
	"R-OBJECT-07": "An asset that moves between the shared and the personal library while it is in an event album moves its files to the root of the other library, one into each directory it needs that holds none of its files, and any left over go by R-OBJECT-04.",
	"R-OBJECT-08": "A move found by content among duplicate files pairs the links of one asset first, then one to one in a fixed order, and an ambiguous one becomes a deletion and a new file with a notice.",
	"R-OBJECT-09": "Of several replacements of one asset in one run only the first by remote priority is made; the others are taken into the base as they are.",
	"R-OBJECT-10": "A matched cloud file that is a lesser copy of the original is replaced by the original under replace_with_original, the copy kept in quarantine.",

	"R-COMPONENT-01": "A Live Photo video or RAW file deleted from the cloud while its main file stays there is restored from iCloud beside the main file where that ends up and beside each copy of the main file, with a warning.",
	"R-COMPONENT-02": "A Live Photo video or RAW file moved away from its main file is moved back beside it, with a warning.",
	"R-COMPONENT-03": "New content in a Live Photo video or RAW file replaces the whole asset with one built from all files of the group.",
	"R-COMPONENT-04": "A Live Photo video, RAW file or sidecar that shares the directory and stem of a main file moves with it and goes to quarantine or leaves the cloud with it by the same action, even when changed itself, or has its link cleared when already gone, and one that the user already put where the main file ends up is taken into the base as it is.",
	"R-COMPONENT-05": "A sidecar changed, moved or deleted on its own does not affect the asset.",

	"R-MODE-01": "An upload-only remote runs only actions toward the cloud, takes the cloud side into the base as it is, only reports new cloud files and detaches the link of a file the user deleted.",
	"R-MODE-02": "A download-only remote runs only actions toward iCloud, takes the iCloud side into the base as it is, does not upload new assets and detaches the link of an asset deleted in iCloud.",
	"R-MODE-03": "A one-way remote has no conflicts, because the side it does not sync always counts as unchanged.",
	"R-MODE-04": "With albums_for_personal set to false, folder changes under the personal root leave iCloud albums as they are and files imported from it join no album.",

	"R-STATUS-01": "With deletes set to quarantine, a cloud file to delete moves to .photosync/quarantine/<date>/<path> under its root and the link becomes quarantined_remote.",
	"R-STATUS-02": "With deletes set to quarantine, an asset to delete goes to Recently Deleted in Photos and its link stays quarantined_icloud while it is there.",
	"R-STATUS-03": "A quarantined link takes no part in the rules for new assets and files, so an asset in Recently Deleted is not uploaded and a quarantined file is not imported.",
	"R-STATUS-04": "An asset or file that the user brings back from quarantine is a change that makes its link active again.",
	"R-STATUS-05": "With deletes set to none, a deletion does not spread and the link stays detached until the user relinks it.",
	"R-STATUS-06": "With deletes set to propagate, a deletion spreads to the other side and the link is removed at once, so a restored asset comes back as a new one.",
	"R-STATUS-07": "A conflict left open by the ask or skip policy is kept across runs and closes by itself once one side returns to the base.",
	"R-STATUS-08": "A replacement keeps the old asset or file in quarantine whatever the deletes policy is.",
	"R-STATUS-09": "A file kept in cloud quarantine longer than quarantine_keep_days is deleted for good.",
	"R-STATUS-10": "With edited_files set to quarantine, a cloud file of an edit, in a directory named in edited_dirs or named as an edited photo, moves to .photosync/quarantine/<date>/<path> under its root without a link, except in a download-only remote.",

	"R-LAYOUT-01": "An album is an event when its folders and title match the Photos template and the cloud template gives it a directory, as it does for an album titled only by its date, and every other album, such as one whose description sanitizing removes whole or, under the default templates, MM/DD with a trailing space, is thematic and does not sync.",
	"R-LAYOUT-02": "The primary placement of an asset is its event album closest to its local capture date, ties going to the album it joined first and then to the first by path, and an asset in no event album has none and, while linked to no file, is skipped with a notice instead of uploaded.",
	"R-LAYOUT-03": "A cloud file whose directory the cloud template does not read as an event, such as one in the root, in a directory above the events or in a directory inside an event directory, unless it is an edit that no link names, is skipped with a notice for its directory and stays as it is, and an asset whose linked file lies there, or has left its path and turns up there by content hash, is frozen in that remote, while a directory paired with an event album is read whatever the cloud template and one paired with a thematic album outside Recently Deleted is skipped the same way.",
	"R-LAYOUT-04": "At the first placement of an asset in several event albums the event closest to its capture date is primary, and the multi_album policy applies once.",
	"R-LAYOUT-05": "An asset in no album, not even a thematic one, joins the only event album of its local capture date while the sync has not linked it to any file, and otherwise has no placement.",
	"R-LAYOUT-06": "A new album pair maps the album path to a directory and back by the year, month, day and description that both templates hold, one level per folder or directory, with no text before an empty description, so the default templates map MM/DD to MM-DD, and with a character that the cloud cannot hold written as a lookalike that is not read back.",
	"R-LAYOUT-07": "The direction of an album pair is fixed by the side where the pair first appeared, so a top-level cloud folder and its album never re-create each other.",
	"R-LAYOUT-08": "Copies of one file in several cloud folders are several links of one asset in several albums, not a conflict.",
	"R-LAYOUT-09": "Each template level above the last is a folder in iCloud and a directory in the cloud and the last is the album, so a directory named only by its date, such as 05-01 under the default templates, reads as an event with an empty description, and a directory deeper than the template, even inside an event directory, reads as no album.",
	"R-LAYOUT-10": "At the first sync an album pairs with an unpaired directory of the same name, else with the one that holds more than half of its matched files, else it gets a new directory.",
	"R-LAYOUT-11": "An album renamed or moved to another folder in iCloud takes its pair and the files of the album that lie directly in it to the directory of its new path when the directory was the one of its old path and the new one is free, so a directory that the user named otherwise keeps its name.",
	"R-LAYOUT-12": "An album directory that the user renames in the cloud within its folders takes the pair of the album along, and the album takes the title that the new name reads as when the directory was named after the album, iCloud kept that path and the remote may add albums there, otherwise only the pair moves.",
	"R-LAYOUT-13": "An album directory that the user moves in the cloud into other folders, where its name reads as the same title, takes the pair of the album along, and when the directory was named after the album, iCloud kept that path and the remote may add albums there, the album moves into the folder of the new path, which the run adds if iCloud lacks it, otherwise only the pair moves.",
	"R-LAYOUT-14": "A directory of a folder of albums that the user renames in the cloud, so that no root holds the old one any more, renames that folder in iCloud with all that it holds, rather than moving its albums, when iCloud has no folder of the new name at that place and an album directory that moved with it was named after its album, iCloud kept that path and the remote may add albums there.",
}
